Description: RE30592 Prāsādaṣaṭślokīvyākhyā. This text contains a commentary (vyākhyā) on six fundamental ślokas that expound the essence of the Prāsādamantra, revered as the supreme and all-encompassing mantra of Lord Śiva. The text elucidates the inner meaning, philosophical depth, and ritual significance of these six verses, presenting the Prāsādamantra as a central doctrinal and contemplative principle within the Śaiva tradition. Through concise explanations, the manuscript bridges mantra theology with metaphysical understanding, highlighting Śiva as the ultimate reality.The manuscript comprises 18 folios, each measuring 3.7 cm × 31.6 cm, written in 6–8 lines per folio. Though brief in extent, the manuscript is of considerable doctrinal value, offering focused insight into one of the most significant Śaiva mantras and its interpretative tradition.
